{"id": "EUVD-2026-103003", "enisaUuid": "ea1c4672-5b8f-311c-a28d-6c04ab573b1f", "description": "Netcore NR256CN through 1.5.140116 contains a pre-authentication stack overflow vulnerability in the Boa web server's user_ok() function, which copies Basic-auth usernames with unbounded strcpy() calls into 64-byte stack buffers. Unauthenticated attackers can send a username longer than 63 bytes to any protected /router/*.cgi route to crash the main Boa process or potentially execute code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:40:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:16:42", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/lukadqq/netcore-router-public-refs/blob/a44d562736b41c944223297e9144d2ad7fa2aff1/2026.10.15-netcore-nr256cn-basic-auth-stack-overflow.md", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netcore-nr256cn-through-1.5.140116-pre-auth-stack-overflow-via-boa-user-ok"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5769-g37j-m8jq", "CVE-2026-111711"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "abf0c1d5-9797-30d7-82b5-d1a1c30ba621", "product": {"name": "NR256CN", "vendor": {"name": "Netcore"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5.140116"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a2fd800a-22ee-3f54-994b-7a26b87877ce", "vendor": {"name": "Netcore"}}], "isExploited": false}